# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# HKOCA QC & Doublet Detection Pipeline - Configuration File
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# ── Global Paths ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Directory containing input .rds files to process
rds_dir: /data-master/pure-workspace/labss/hmami/new_data/rds_files

# Path to the CSV file defining QC thresholds for each sample
decisions_csv: /data-master/pure-workspace/labss/hmami/new_data/HKOCA-tools/scripts/qc/QC_Decisions.csv

# Base directory where results (Summary, Filtered RDS, Logs) will be saved
output_dir: /data-master/pure-workspace/labss/hmami/new_data/HKOCA-tools/scripts/qc/qc_results_try

# ── Output Subdirectories ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# (Relative to output_dir)
summary_subdir: Summary
filtered_subdir: qc_filtered_rds
doublet_subdir: doublet_filtered_rds
log_file: logs/qc_run.log

# ── Processing Filters ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# File pattern to search for in rds_dir
rds_pattern: \.rds$

# Search in subfolders of rds_dir?
recursive_discovery: FALSE

# Safety flag to skip datasets known to be low quality or problematic
skip_noisy_datasets: TRUE

# List of basenames to explicitly skip (one per line, comma or space separated)
noisy_datasets:

# ── scDblFinder Parameters ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Batch column for doublet detection (usually donor or sample)
dbl_batch_col: sample_id

# Hard filters before doublet detection (prevents noise from skewing estimates)
dbl_min_count: 100
dbl_min_feature: 50

# PC dimensions for UMAP/Clustering internal to scDblFinder
dbl_umap_dims: 20

# Default chemistry if not specified in overrides below
dbl_default_platform: 10x

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PER-SAMPLE OVERRIDES
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If a sample requires a specific platform or a fixed doublet rate (dbr),
# define them here using the convention: 
#   sample.<BASENAME>.platform: <platform>
#   sample.<BASENAME>.dbr: <numeric>
#
# Examples (Uncomment to use):
# sample.MY_SAMPLE_A.platform: 10x
# sample.MY_SAMPLE_A.dbr: 0.08
# sample.MY_SAMPLE_B.platform: dropseq
# sample.MY_SAMPLE_B.dbr: 0.05
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
